        "id": 1002970
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-27T07:52:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Each read gets its own 120 s window, and devices are created one after another\n(initDevices() and interfaceAddedMatch() both co_await handleInterfaceAdded()\nin a loop). If Entity-Manager is down rather than briefly busy, one device can\nspend 120 s here, then another 120 s in each dbusGetRequiredProperty() call in\ninitDevice(), and so on. A daemon with N devices then needs several minutes per\ndevice to start, and interfaceAddedMatch() stops consuming InterfacesAdded\nsignals while it retries.\n\nCould the budget be shared (one deadline per device or per initial scan), or\ncould each device be spawned (ctx.spawn) so a slow device does not block the\nothers?",
      "revId": "fb172ce403ab67332aba2dbe3d7e5dd00749a6ca",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
